WEBVTT

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:11.610
Commercial Lending
A corporate facility from the RM's request to an active, monitored loan — memo, spreading, approval and covenants on one record.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:20.040
Port Louis Logistics Ltd needs a MUR 15 million working-capital line
A bigger fleet and new contracts — the corporate RM opens the request

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:26.520
Sign in as Bruno Chan — Relationship Manager (Corporate)
Corporate relationship manager — owns the facility

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:37.400
Commercial Lending ▸ Commercial facility request
A two-step guided form for the RM

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:49.080
Amount, tenor and pricing
Margin over the Genesis PLR, arrangement and commitment fees

00:00:49.080 --> 00:01:00.360
CF-2026-000024 is created at Origination and assigned to the corporate RM
Interest rate = Genesis PLR + margin · approval authority from the amount

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:09.012
Group exposure: every facility of the Doorga Group — now including this one
Checked against the group lending limit before credit takes it on

00:01:09.012 --> 00:01:18.080
The RM moves the request to RM assessment
Then tries to send it on to Credit memo…

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.600
Blocked: the credit memo needs the company background and the security package
The board says exactly what is missing

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:33.720
Write the memo on its own form
Edit ▸ Credit memo tab — the same record, a focused form

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:38.360
Memo written — Credit memo now accepts the facility

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:45.040
The credit analyst spreads two years of audited accounts
Commercial Lending ▸ Financial Spread ▸ New — one row per financial year

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:59.840
Sign in as Nadia Peerbux — Credit Analyst
Credit analyst — spreads the financials and grades the risk

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:13.240
FY 2025: the latest audited year

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:17.623
The ratios are calculated for every year
EBITDA margin · DSCR · net debt / EBITDA · gearing · interest cover

00:02:21.354 --> 00:02:28.868
Back on the facility: the latest DSCR and leverage are read from the spread
The analyst sets the internal risk grade and writes the recommendation

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:43.417
Credit approval needs a recommendation and a risk grade
Try it first…

00:02:43.417 --> 00:02:53.563
Who approves? Masters ▸ Approval Matrices
Lending bands: up to MUR 5m Loans Manager · up to MUR 20m Credit Committee · above, the Board Credit Committee

00:02:53.563 --> 00:02:59.483
MUR 15 million falls in the Credit Committee band
Moving to Credit approval raises the approval request

00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:05.003
The Credit Committee decides
Tools ▸ Approvals — the request carries amount, grade and DSCR

00:03:05.003 --> 00:03:18.423
Sign in as Jean-Marc Desvaux — Credit Committee Member
Credit committee member — approves facilities up to MUR 20 million

00:03:18.423 --> 00:03:25.103
Approved — the facility moved itself to Term sheet / offer
Credit decision: Approved

00:03:25.103 --> 00:03:33.143
The term sheet was generated and filed on the Docs tab
Amount, tenor, pricing, fees and the security package — ready to send to the borrower

00:03:33.143 --> 00:03:40.358
Preview the term sheet
Facility, amount, tenor, pricing and fees — filled in from the record

00:03:40.358 --> 00:03:45.998
The borrower signs the term sheet
The RM registers the charges and guarantee — Security perfection

00:03:45.998 --> 00:03:57.278
Sign in as Bruno Chan — Relationship Manager (Corporate)
Corporate relationship manager

00:03:57.278 --> 00:04:02.718
Active: the CRM checks the borrower's KYC is approved
Port Louis Logistics Ltd's KYC is approved — the facility goes live

00:04:04.438 --> 00:04:14.598
Record the covenants the committee set
Commercial Lending ▸ Covenant ▸ New

00:04:14.598 --> 00:04:26.758
A year on: management accounts show DSCR at 1.08x
Covenant Test ▸ New — record the actual value

00:04:26.758 --> 00:04:33.838
1.08 is below the 1.25 threshold: the result is Breach
The RM and the Loans Manager are alerted at once

00:04:33.838 --> 00:04:39.518
The facility counts its covenants in breach
Watch-list reporting and the Loan Book dashboard read the same figure

00:04:39.518 --> 00:04:43.638
The Loans Manager gets the breach alert
He decides on a waiver or a remedy

00:04:43.638 --> 00:04:51.558
Sign in as Rajiv Doorgakant — Manager, Loans & Fixed Income
Manager, Loans & Fixed Income — decides covenant waivers

00:04:51.558 --> 00:05:00.432
Notifications: “Covenant breach” with the actual value and threshold

00:05:00.432 --> 00:05:06.003
Waiver granted and the terms recorded on the test
The next test date stays in the calendar for the RM

00:05:06.003 --> 00:05:13.592
Commercial Lending
Four people worked one facility — the CRM checked every gate and routed every decision.
